> Using here {le nanmu} is not better and actually it might be wrong.

There is no way something like that is _wrong_. It makes more assumptions
about the existence of an entity you call {le nanmu} (more than {lo}),
but it makes _less_ assumptions about properties of that entity.

That is to say, if that entity you refer to exists, and you are actually
trying to refer to it, then there is no way the {le} version is wrong
and {lo} is not.

